<div class="hero"><span class="flag">🇲🇾</span><h1>From Malaysia to China: Advanced Care, Lower Prices</h1><p>For cancer treatment, cardiac surgery and joint replacement, China's JCI-accredited and Grade 3A hospitals typically cost 20–40% less than Malaysian private hospitals — with shorter waits for radiotherapy and procedures that are not routinely available at home.</p><a href="/contact-new.html?source=malaysia-landing" class="btn-red">Start Free Case Review &rarr;</a></div>

<div class="card"><h2>Cost Comparison: China vs Malaysia (2026)</h2>
<table><tr><th>Procedure</th><th>China</th><th>Malaysia (private)</th><th>Savings</th></tr>
<tr><td>Heart Bypass (CABG)</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$10K-$16K</td><td>$14K-$20K</td><td style="color:#2e7d32">20-30%</td></tr>
<tr><td>Valve Replacement</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$12K-$20K</td><td>$16K-$26K</td><td style="color:#2e7d32">20-25%</td></tr>
<tr><td>Angioplasty + 1 Stent</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$4.5K-$8K</td><td>$6K-$11K</td><td style="color:#2e7d32">25-30%</td></tr>
<tr><td>Knee Replacement</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$5.5K-$9K</td><td>$9K-$15K</td><td style="color:#2e7d32">35-40%</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hip Replacement</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$6.5K-$10K</td><td>$10K-$16K</td><td style="color:#2e7d32">35-40%</td></tr>
<tr><td>Spinal Fusion (1-2 levels)</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$8K-$14K</td><td>$12K-$20K</td><td style="color:#2e7d32">30-35%</td></tr>
<tr><td>CAR-T Therapy</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$30K-$89K</td><td>Limited availability</td><td style="color:#2e7d32">Access</td></tr></table>
<p style="font-size:.85rem;color:#888">Prices are 2026 estimates for total in-hospital cost. Malaysia's private hospitals are affordable by global standards and remain the right choice for routine care — patients travel to China mainly for <strong>complex or high-capacity procedures</strong>, where cost and waiting time both differ. Final cost depends on hospital and clinical complexity. See the full <a href="/compare/" style="color:#1e3c72;font-weight:600">China vs Thailand vs Malaysia comparison</a>.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h2>Why Malaysian Patients Choose China for Treatment</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Short direct flights:</strong> Kuala Lumpur to Guangzhou is about 4 hours, and to Beijing or Shanghai about 6 hours, with daily departures on Malaysia Airlines, AirAsia and China Southern.</li><li><strong>Cancer capacity:</strong> China's largest radiotherapy networks schedule a full chemoradiation course within weeks. For treatments such as CAR-T, availability in Malaysia is limited.</li><li><strong>English-speaking staff:</strong> All recommended hospitals have international departments that work in English.</li><li><strong>Muslim-friendly care:</strong> Several recommended hospitals provide halal meals and prayer rooms — worth confirming for your chosen hospital during the case review.</li><li><strong>JCI accreditation:</strong> Top Chinese hospitals meet the same standards as leading US and Singapore academic centres.</li><li><strong>Visa-free entry:</strong> Malaysia is covered by China's visa-free arrangements for short stays. Rules and duration change, so check the <a href="/visa-guide.html" style="color:#1e3c72;font-weight:600">visa guide</a> for the current policy.</li><li><strong>Start small with imaging:</strong> Not ready for surgery? Book an <a href="/medical-imaging.html" style="color:#1e3c72;font-weight:600">MRI or CT scan</a> from $150 — scheduled within 24–48 hours.</li></ul></div>

<div class="card"><h2>How We Help Malaysian Patients</h2><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Tell us your condition, records, and timing — free, no commitment.</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> We review your case at no cost and name the one hospital we would point you to, with a cost comparison and visa guidance.</p><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> We coordinate records, appointments, invitation letters, and airport pickup. You fly from Kuala Lumpur — we handle the rest.</p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> Free case review to start. $199 to have us contact two hospitals and bring back their answers in writing, $649 for full journey management. No hidden fees, no hospital commissions. <a href="/pricing.html">See pricing →</a></p></div>

